xchange using language-specific vocabulary confirmed by the teacher and compare expression, tone and courtesy."],"resources":"Fluent community-language recording, picture prompts and pair-speaking cards.","assessment":"Teacher observes attentive recall, authentic local-language vocabulary and respectful oral interaction, using a simple three-point checklist.","competencies":"Communication and collaboration; creativity; critical thinking; self-efficacy; cultural identity; digital literacy where permitted.","reviewStatus":"language_adaptation_required"},{"id":"02-RD","theme":2,"themeTitle":"Weather","sourcePage":7,"strand":"Reading","title":"Weather: Reading Fluency","focus":"Reading Fluency","focusDetail":"Weather forecasts, expressive pace and intonation","lessons":2,"crossStrand":false,"outcomes":["Read a spoken-style weather bulletin with changes of pace in the selected indigenous language, attending to weather forecasts, expressive pace and intonation.","Locate and explain two details from the reading and support an interpretation with words from the text.","Explain a new word, proverb or expression through context or confirmation with a fluent language user."],"inquiry":["How can a reader understand weather from words and surrounding clues?","What does the text reveal about how this community uses language?"],"experiences":["Use a locally verified short text about rainfall, sunshine and preparing for changing weather; learners mark familiar words, predict meaning and reread for accuracy.","Pairs discuss a comprehension question and practise correct pacing or interpretation with a fluent speaker's feedback."],"resources":"Original or licensed local-language passage, bilingual picture clues and reader's notebook.","assessment":"Reading aloud or assisted reading plus two text-based questions and a short explanation of a locally verified expression.","competencies":"Communication and collaboration; creativity; critical thinking; self-efficacy; cultural identity; dig